{/* §2.7 POSITION 7 — TABLE CARD. The section is now a plain paper-surface container
    holding the single bounded card the table already lived in, rather than another
    full-bleed tinted band. Position 5 is a full-bleed grid and 6 is a divided band, so
    a third band here would be the run §2.7 exists to break.

    IT ALSO REMOVES AN AA FAILURE — but not the one first diagnosed, and the distinction
    is the useful part of this comment.

    The failing pair was the section LEDE (`text-gray`, --color-gray #6e675c), which sat
    directly on the old `bg-[#12100C]/60` surface. 60% dark over the paper page
    composites to roughly #55534e, and grey-on-grey measured **1.05:1** against a 4.5
    requirement — effectively invisible, and the worst pair on the homepage by a wide
    margin. On the paper surface the same colour is 5.09:1.

    The table CELLS (#A79E8C) were never the problem. They are inside the opaque
    #1B1811 card and measure 6.68:1 — passing before this change and unchanged by it.
    An earlier pass reported them as the 2.00:1 failure by compositing them against the
    section tint instead of the card they actually sit in. Recorded because the mistake
    is easy to repeat: when a section is translucent, WHICH element a colour sits on
    decides the result, and the nearest opaque ancestor is the one that counts. */}
